				<CaseStructure.Selector Bounds="-4 725 13 10" Docking="Left" Id="65" Terminals="62=1091, 63=632, 64=643" />
				<CaseStructure.Tunnel Bounds="1816 865 13 10" Docking="Right" Id="66" Terminals="62=645, 63=641, 64=642" />
			</CaseStructure>
			<Comment Bounds="2900 1185 1985 150" Id="495" SizeToText="False" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/MocCommon">
				<p.Text>"1. Initialize Globals for UI Control References, TestStand Manager Controls, Menu, and Tab \n2. Set Globals for Top Level VI and Control Borders. Check that control references are valid before trying to do any property node calls on them\n3. Wait in Main Event Loop until user clicks the Close box on the front panel window or the Quit Application Event is fired.\n4. handle user menu selections asynchronously so the UI is not blocked\n5. If the ShutDown method returns True, then the user interface can continue with shutting down. If not, continue handlngi events to wait for the Quit Application Event.\n6. Disable Panel Updates to speed drawing by preventing drawing intermediate states.\r\n\r\nTo modify the installed user interfaces or to create new user interfaces, modify the files in the &lt;TestStand Public&gt;\\UserInterfaces directory. You can use the read-only source files for the default user interfaces in the &lt;TestStand&gt;\\UserInterfaces directory as a reference. National Instruments recommends that you track the changes you make to the user interface source code files so you can integrate the changes with any enhancements in future versions of the TestStand User Interfaces."</p.Text>
			</Comment>
			<Comment Bounds="2900 45 970 90" Id="497" SizeToText="False" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/MocCommon">
				<p.Text>"This is the main VI in the full-featured user interface. Note that this VI runs in the User Interface execution system to optimize its performance and allow TestStand dialogs to\nhave correct modality behavior. Its subVIs are configured to run in the same execution system as their callers. \n\nNote:\tThis UI can function as an editor or an operator interface. The user can change the edit mode with a keystroke (ctrl+alt+shift+insert) or with a command line \nargument. For more information and for instructions on how prevent the user from changing the edit mode, refer to the Creating Editor Applications topic in the TestStand help \n\n"</p.Text>
			</Comment>
			<Wire Id="645" Joints="N(66:62)|(4799,1010) N(60:Value)|(4828,1010)" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/PlatformFramework" />
			<InitializeUIControls Bounds="2920 835 40 40" Id="1090" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/TestStand.Control" />
			<Wire Id="1091" Joints="N(1090:error out)|(2960,870) N(65:62)|(2966,870)" xmlns="http://www.ni.com/PlatformFramework" />
		</BlockDiagram>
